task: staged-runtime
agent: fable-persist
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/staged-runtime
worktree: ../okay-wt-staging

why: the operator's call, 2026-09-07 ("Сделай рантайм стейджинг и
  подумай где еще он может быть полезен"), after the case for and
  against was laid out: the fold over Schema runs in two modes,
  interpreted and staged at compile time (5-6x on decode/encode);
  schemas that exist only at run time — Pg composites from the
  catalog, tool specs from an MCP server, a JSON-frame from R/Python —
  have only the interpreter.

what: okay-staging, a JVM-only opt-in module over okay-codec with
  the scala3-staging dependency: `RuntimeStaged.json(schema)` runs the
  SAME generator over a Schema VALUE inside `staging.run`, one
  persistent Compiler, a cache per schema, the generated codec
  agreeing with the interpreter byte-for-byte and Left-for-Left over
  the whole node vocabulary (the TestStaged agreement suite, run over
  run-time-built schemas). Measured in `compare` against the
  interpreter and the compile-time staged codec on the same shape —
  the first-use compile cost and the steady-state gain both in the
  table. A spec section lists where else a run-time schema is hot
  enough to matter, with the condition for each, and where it is not.
